sequenceDiagram
    actor User as CLI User
    participant BIC as ImageBuildSubcommand
    participant RIB as RunnerImageBuild
    participant RIR as RunnerImageRenderer
    participant IBS as ImageBuilderService
    participant CF as AWS CloudFormation
    participant EC2 as AWS EC2
    participant IB as AWS Image Builder
    participant SSM as AWS SSM
    participant S3 as AWS S3

    User->>BIC: baas admin image build [--extension ext.yaml]
    Note over BIC: Invocation.configService(spec).load() -- requirePrefix, resolveRegion
    opt --extension
        Note over BIC: not a regular file -> exit 1. RunnerImageExtension.parse strips the<br/>baas-extension-base marker, requireStorable refuses what the stack could not hold<br/>(over 4096 bytes, non-ASCII) -> exit 1 before any AWS call
    end
    Note over BIC: DeployerSession.factory(config) -- deployer credentials, never the operator role:<br/>imagebuilder, ssm:PutParameter and a widened iam:PassRole
    BIC->>RIB: run(factory, prefix, region, pushed)
    RIB->>RIR: definition(), renderBase()
    RIR-->>RIB: base imageVersion, parentImage.amiName, base AWSTOE document

    RIB->>CF: CloudFormationService.stackExists, getStackParameters(prefix)
    alt no stack
        RIB-->>BIC: IllegalStateException naming admin deployment setup -- exit 1
    end
    Note over RIB: olderBaseRefusal: bundled base lower than the deployed RunnerImageVersion -><br/>refused, naming both and the CLI upgrade, nothing submitted
    opt --extension
        Note over RIB: RunnerImageExtension.requireCurrent -- the file's marker must name the deployed<br/>extension. The stack holds the only copy. No extension deployed -> any file is accepted.
    end
    RIB->>EC2: ParentImageResolver.resolve(amiName, region) -- describeImages, owner amazon
    EC2-->>RIB: exactly one image in this region, else refused
    Note over RIB: RunnerImageParameters.plan: label = base or base+ext.sha256[0:8],<br/>contract rendered with the label, the bucket and the region, extension and recipe versions derived from the deployed stack

    RIB->>IBS: preflightVersion(<prefix>-component-runner, baseVersion, base)
    IBS->>IB: listComponents(owner Self, filter name) -- deliberately WITHOUT byName
    opt the base version is already registered
        IBS->>IB: listComponentBuildVersions + getComponent
        Note over IBS: content differs (trailing whitespace forgiven) -> refused:<br/>bump imageVersion in infra/runner-image.yaml. Nothing is submitted.
    end

    RIB->>CF: updateStackParameters(prefix, coreTemplate, plan.values())
    Note over RIB,CF: every image parameter is sent, every other declared one carried forward<br/>with UsePreviousValue, so CI's federation survives
    RIB->>CF: getStackOutputs -> RunnerImagePipelineArn (missing -> refused)

    RIB->>IBS: publish(pipelineArn, /<prefix>/runner/ami-id, label, parentAmiId, recipeVersion, bucket)
    IBS->>SSM: readPointer -- the AMI being replaced, if any
    IBS->>IB: listImagePipelineImages -- newest build of the pipeline (adoptOrBuild)
    alt newest build in progress, same recipe version
        Note over IBS: wait for it instead of starting another
    else newest build in progress, superseded recipe
        Note over IBS: wait for it to end, retire its AMI, then build
    else newest build succeeded, same recipe, unpublished AMI still exists
        Note over IBS: adopt it -- no new build
    else otherwise (an unpublished superseded AMI is retired first)
        IBS->>IB: startImagePipelineExecution(pipelineArn)
        IB-->>IBS: imageBuildVersionArn
    end
    Note over IB,EC2: Image Builder bakes the base, the extension, then the contract,<br/>snapshots the AMI and runs the contract's test phase on a booted instance.<br/>The test phase checks every /opt/jdks entry and writes image-builds/label/jdks.json
    loop await, every 30 s
        IBS->>IB: getImage(imageBuildVersionArn)
        IB-->>IBS: in progress, AVAILABLE, or failed
    end
    alt failed
        Note over IBS: retireFailedOutput -- a test-stage failure leaves a registered AMI,<br/>so it is deregistered here. Throws with Image Builder's reason, pointer untouched.
        IBS-->>BIC: exit 1
    end
    IBS->>EC2: ensureIdentityTags -- describeImages, createTags(baas-image-version, baas-parent-ami) if absent
    IBS->>S3: tagJdks -- getObject image-builds/label/jdks.json, the list the contract wrote
    alt list missing or malformed
        Note over IBS: retire the new AMI. Throws naming the key, pointer untouched.
        IBS-->>BIC: exit 1
    end
    IBS->>EC2: createTags(baas-jdks = the ids, default first) -- before the pointer moves
    IBS->>SSM: writePointer -- putParameter(/<prefix>/runner/ami-id = newAmiId)
    Note over IBS,SSM: REPOINT BEFORE RETIRE. Deregistering first would aim the pointer<br/>at a deleted AMI for the whole build, failing every job launched in that window.
    opt a replaced AMI that differs from the new one
        IBS->>EC2: retire -- describeImages (snapshot ids), deregisterImage, deleteSnapshot each
        Note over IBS: retireQuietly -- a failure is a warning, the new image is already published
    end
    IBS-->>RIB: newAmiId
    RIB-->>BIC: Result(amiId, label, parentAmiId, extension, pointer)
    BIC-->>User: label, AMI, parent, extension identity, pointer -- exit 0
